From: waveydude <23585435+waveydude@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] common: release task captures before reporting completion

Port the worker cleanup ordering from zortos293/Lichii#1105 and #939.
Keep capture destruction outside queue_mutex.

Taken unchanged from waveydude's tree (issue 21, 10 Nov 2026; his commit c593ef4, where the file
is 0487-lichii-1105-worker-cleanup.patch: renumbered, our 0487 is another patch).

diff --git a/src/common/thread_worker.h b/src/common/thread_worker.h
--- a/src/common/thread_worker.h
+++ b/src/common/thread_worker.h
@@ -78,6 +78,8 @@ class StatefulThreadWorker {
                     } else {
                         task();
                     }
+                    // Draining an executed task includes releasing its captured resources.
+                    task = {};
                     ++work_done;
                 }
             }
